{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/848209-homebrew-cryptids-and-adaptations","id":848209,"title":"Homebrew Cryptids and Adaptations","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-03-16T08:54:32-07:00","id":848209,"title":"Homebrew Cryptids and Adaptations","content":"Here's your one stop shop for all crowd-sourced, home(micro)brewed Cryptids and Adaptations. We'll try to assemble everything in this post, once finalized, for easy viewing. And/Or create a Google Doc for copying. Feel free to cross-post any Cryptids you may already have, or just discuss and development them below.<br /> <hr /><br /> [Placeholder for finished Adaptations]<br /> <hr /><br /> [Placeholder for finished Cryptids]","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T09:07:16-07:00","id":848214,"title":"","content":"[Personal placeholder for the following ideas]<br /> <br /> &lt;Angel Eater - Adaptation - Based on Ghost Eater and Essence Thief, but targeted towards Angels&gt;<br /> <br /> &lt;Aether Dependency - Adaptation - Models Hellhounds Aether needs as an Adaptation&gt;<br /> <br /> &lt;Soul Eater #1 - Cryptid - Thing that eats Cover Elements/Dots, or parts of a human's Pact-able features when Covers aren't available.&gt;<br /> <br /> &lt;Soul Eater #2 - Cryptid - Human -&gt; Stigmatic -&gt; Grafted to Form Gadget -&gt; Cryptid, that needs to eat others' souls (Soul-less Condition) to alleviate their own Soul-less Condition&gt;<br /> <br /> &lt;Blood of Creation - Adaptation - Develop for certain Aurel Cryptids, Cryptid's blood/remains can Install an Embed or Exploit into an object&gt;<br /> <br /> &lt;Death Curse - Adaptation - Reflexively uses an Exploit upon the Cryptid's death - note: not limited to harmful Exploits&gt;<br /> <br /> &lt;Aether Transference - Adaptation - Allows Cryptid to transfer Aether to and from sources&gt;<br /> <br /> &lt;Aether Collector - Adaptation - Cryptid can gather ambient Aether, like Demon-Blooded, for use or storage&gt;<br /> <br /> &lt;Symbiosis - Adaptation - Material version of the Claim Manifestation&gt;<br /> <br /> &lt;Aether Beatles - Cryptid - Moves around, storing spare Aether into Stockpiles like a squirrel stores nuts. Used to explain why Exploited Gadgets might not have decayed after long periods left alone.&gt;<br /> <br /> &lt;Deal Maker - Adaptation - Allows the Cryptid to make Pacts with other similar to a Demon. Might not need documents, however.&gt;<br /> <br /> &lt;Accursed Bite - Adaptation - Attacks from the Cryptid inflict Glitches upon targets (even non-Demons). Not restricted solely to bite attacks, despite the name.&gt;<br /> <br /> &lt;Legion - Adaptation - Cryptid is merely one part of a larger creature. Can be used to represent appendages, avatar manifestations, hive-minds, etc.&gt;<br /> <br /> &lt;Imprinting - Adaptation - Material version of the Fetter Manifestation&gt;<br /> <br /> &lt;Tiresiades - Cryptid - Aurelian Cryptid. Mad, Blind Seers sought out for advice despite the costs&gt;<br /> <br /> &lt;Veykhas - Cryptid - Aurelian Cryptid. Collector of lost things. Can recreate objects and even people lost, for a price&gt;<br /> <br /> &lt;Kerberan Hound - Cryptid - Aurelian Cryptid. Spotted canine, only a little smaller than an adult human. Fierce guardians who Imprint (via Imprinting) upon their wards. Ahk variants are particularly prized for possessing Amorphous as well.&gt;<br /> <br /> &lt;Inhabit Mask - Adaptation - Cryptid can assume pre-existing Covers&gt;<br /> <br /> &lt;Myth-Weaver - Cryptid - Uses a combination of Urban Legend (as Adaptation) and Inhabit Mask to spin stories and dramas to feed off of.&gt;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 03-29-2016, 11:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T07:36:24-07:00","id":848783,"title":"","content":"Cross Contamination of Hybrid? (Adaptation) - Cryptids can take on characteristics/abilities of other supernaturals.<br /> <br /> Nest (Adaptation) - A Cryptid form of a Bolthole. <br /> <br /> Spawning Cycle (Adaptation) - A multi level adaptation that determines how quickly a Cryptid can reproduce.<br /> <br /> Myth (Adaptation) - Local legends and superstition surround the Cryptid giving it access to its own version of Legend.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10394-lladas","name":"lladas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T09:08:13-07:00","id":859680,"title":"","content":"Hmm. I'm thinking of making an Adaptation for allowing a Cryptid to count as Mortal (such as for picking up Supernatural Merits, and Abjuration, etc.), but I'm not sure it is even really necessary? Thoughts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-06T09:18:03-07:00","id":860360,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/848209-homebrew-cryptids-and-adaptations?p=859680#post859680\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm. I'm thinking of making an Adaptation for allowing a Cryptid to count as Mortal (such as for picking up Supernatural Merits, and Abjuration, etc.), but I'm not sure it is even really necessary? Thoughts?</div> </div> </div> </div>I like the idea of it. I could see it being used for those cryptids who hide among humanity. Maybe it would allow them access to social merits. I am curious why you would want them to be mortal to pick up supernatural merits when you could make adaptions to cover them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10394-lladas","name":"lladas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-06T13:03:51-07:00","id":860511,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lladas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/848209-homebrew-cryptids-and-adaptations?p=860360#post860360\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I like the idea of it. I could see it being used for those cryptids who hide among humanity. Maybe it would allow them access to social merits. I am curious why you would want them to be mortal to pick up supernatural merits when you could make adaptions to cover them?</div> </div> </div> </div>I've got notes/plans for a Demon Shard/Setting, which is basically a standard-ish Fantasy setting (baring the &quot;Gods&quot; being potent Demons, and the world being stitched together from Infrastructure-folded space) - this would have been for Elf/Dwarf/Whatever-equivalents, if desired. Model them as a Rank 1-2 Cryptid (for inherent traits), but are otherwise mortal. They'd only have the Adaptations inherent to their &quot;race&quot;, but have to pick up other Merits as normal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 04-07-2016, 06:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-06T14:37:07-07:00","id":860559,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/848209-homebrew-cryptids-and-adaptations?p=860511#post860511\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I've got notes/plans for a Demon Shard/Setting, which is basically a standish Fantasy setting (baring the &amp;quot;Gods&amp;quot; being potent Demons, and the world being stitched together from Infrastructure-folded space) - this would have been for Elf/Dwarf/Whatever-equivalents, if desired. Model them as a Rank 1-2 Cryptid (for inherent traits), but are otherwise mortal. They'd only have the Adaptations inherent to their &amp;quot;race&amp;quot;, but have to pick up other Merits as normal.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, that is an amazing idea. Reading that then I think you can just set it up that they can pick up merits per usual. That rule could just pertain to that shard and I don't see how you would have much issue from there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10394-lladas","name":"lladas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T09:05:02-07:00","id":923885,"title":"","content":"&lt;eMauler - Cryptid - A Badger &quot;enhanced&quot; with Hellhounds Exploit to have at least the Data-Form (Demonic Form) Adaptation, for when you need to maul someone over the internet.&gt;<br /> <br /> &lt;Modulus - Cryptid - An amorphous blob with the Amorphous (Demonic Form) Adaptation, letting it, well, adapt to whatever it needs (at least, Demonic Form-wise).&gt;<br /> <br /> &lt;Hunter-Seeker - Cryptid - A bloodhound with at least Tag &amp; Release (Embed), Rip The Gates (Exploit), and Special Someone (Embed) as Adaptations, for tracking a target <i>wherever</i> they hide.&gt;<br /> <br /> &lt;Deal Maker - Adaptation - Cryptid can make Pacts just like a Demon can. Most don't use Cover (though ones with Inhabit Mask can), but some &quot;eat&quot; these elements, and while Demon's can't get Benefits as Assets, nothing says Cryptids can't. Penalties for destroyed/broken Pacts remain and if the Cryptid lacks Cover, it always takes the damage itself.&gt;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 06-30-2016, 12:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T11:54:21-07:00","id":923998,"title":"","content":"Since cryptids can have adaptations based on such a wide variety of powers why not also look at the horror section for inspiration?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T12:09:30-07:00","id":924007,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.F.I.X.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/848209-homebrew-cryptids-and-adaptations?p=923998#post923998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since cryptids can have adaptations based on such a wide variety of powers why not also look at the horror section for inspiration?</div> </div> </div> </div>What do you mean?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T14:59:06-07:00","id":924117,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/848209-homebrew-cryptids-and-adaptations?p=924007#post924007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What do you mean?</div> </div> </div> </div>The core book for CofD that was released after demon had been has a section for horrors, generic monsters. They have some unique and interesting powers. I'm just concidering if a cryptid could have adaptations based on the powers those horrors have.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T15:50:13-07:00","id":924146,"title":"","content":"You mean the Dread Powers? I'd think so. They can have Supernatural Merits, Demonic Form Abilities, and Numina as it is. Why not Dread Powers?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T17:26:32-07:00","id":924189,"title":"","content":"Oh right they did call them dread powers. I was wracking my brain trying to remember what they were called n thought that dread powers was wring because hunter often uses that term.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-01T09:18:04-07:00","id":924491,"title":"","content":"Hunter used it first, in 1E. Then Vampire 2E used it for Strix, and Werewolf 2E for Idigam, <i>then</i> CofD Core for the general Horrors section.<br /> <br /> &lt;Illuminated Guardians - Cryptid - Used to protect older tomes and manuscripts, these Cryptids possess Collapsible and [the 2D Demonic Form Ability] to hide themselves in the illuminated artwork of books, until an intruder tries to read a restricted section. Then they become fully sized and 3D, and attack.&gt; <hr /><br /> Now I'm wondering if you could do a &quot;Kryptonian&quot; as a Cryptid? Laser Cutter for Heat Vision, Inhuman Strength, Wings (modded for unsourced, general flight), Armor... even give them a Bane to a particular form of rock/radiation...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 07-01-2016, 12:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-06T09:41:21-07:00","id":927134,"title":"","content":"This was a bit of Infrastructure that I created, which included some new cryptoflora. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/456851-golden-savanna-a-setting-for-demon-including-new-cryptoflora\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/456851-golden-savanna-a-setting-for-demon-including-new-cryptoflora\"> Golden Savanna - A setting for Demon, including new cryptoflora - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/456851-golden-savanna-a-setting-for-demon-including-new-cryptoflora\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/456851-golden-savanna-a-setting-for-demon-including-new-cryptoflora </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Six months ago, I wrote up this setting and sent it in for the open call for writers. Since I never heard back from them, I reasoned that this one probably didn't catch their attention. I liked it enough, though, that I thought I'd put it up here so that other Demon Storytellers might get a little use out </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-06T10:04:35-07:00","id":927144,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/848209-homebrew-cryptids-and-adaptations?p=927134#post927134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This was a bit of Infrastructure that I created, which included some new cryptoflora.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/456851-golden-savanna-a-setting-for-demon-including-new-cryptoflora\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...ew-cryptoflora</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Looks interesting...<br /> <br /> Reading that game me the idea for one kind of Cryptoflora (well, Cryptofungi) - mushrooms that enable Animal Communication when eaten (to represent such fairy tales). Actually, you might have an entire grouping/line of edible Cryptoflora that produces Gadget-like effects when eaten - healing moss (On the Mend), psychotropic plants (Visions of Heaven and Hell), Forget-me-Lots (Unperson), etc.<br /> <br /> Hmm.<br /> &lt;Death-thorn - Cryptoflora - These thorny vines infect those who are pricked by them with an Ultimatum to care for the plant and bring it food for a day - or they turn into &quot;fertilizer&quot;. Of course, caring for the vines often leads to additional pricks, which resets the Ultimatum...&gt;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}